# Global QA wake (all projects)

Kit home: `~/Documents/QA-kit/` (or `~/Documents/cursor-qa`)  
Read `~/Documents/QA-kit/WAKE.md` and `~/Documents/QA-kit/RULES.md`.

## Resolve QA_ROOT first (every wake)

```bash
QA_ROOT=$(bash ~/Documents/QA-kit/tools/resolve-qa-root.sh "$(pwd)" 2>/dev/null \
  || bash ~/Documents/cursor-qa/tools/resolve-qa-root.sh "$(pwd)")
echo "$QA_ROOT"
```

If the project is new, resolve/init creates `projects/<folder-name>/` under the kit.

Shared:

- Credentials: `$QA_ROOT/credentials.local.yaml` (message overrides win)
- Devices: `bash $KIT/tools/pick-devices.sh` (up to 5) or `pick-device.sh`
- Write **only** `$QA_ROOT/results/` and `$QA_ROOT/reports/` (learn agent may write `catalog/drafts/`)
- Prefer project agents under `$QA_ROOT/agents/`; else kit `agents/`
- **Never** edit product source as part of QA

---

## A) Release / full (parallel when devices allow)

> make a apk release build and wake up the QA agent

Optional in the same message: `profile: smoke|changed|full`, `devices: s1,s2,...`, credential overrides.

1. Build release for **this** workspace  
2. Orchestrator: `$QA_ROOT/agents/00-orchestrator.md` or kit `00-orchestrator.md`  
3. Plan: `plan-run.sh` → parallel `10-shard-worker` when 2+ devices  
4. Merge shards → reporter → Excel / live guide if tools exist  
5. `run_id` = `YYYYMMDD-HHMM-release` (or `-smoke` / `-changed`)

## B) Debug / screen

> wake up the agent and QA this screen and its widgets (FILE) (WHAT_TO_QA)

1. Debug mode — no release build required  
2. Agent: `$QA_ROOT/agents/08-screen-debug.md` or kit `08-screen-debug.md`  
3. `run_id` = `YYYYMMDD-HHMM-debug-<screen>`

## C) Promote draft (human)

> promote QA draft DRAFT-…

Runs `promote-draft.sh` — drafts are not official until promoted.

## After run

- `merge-shards.mjs` if shard folders exist
- Reporter / Excel if tools exist under `$QA_ROOT/tools/`
- If `$QA_ROOT/tools/ensure-live-guide.sh` exists, run it with `run_id`
